  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n Want to Make a Seller Hate You? Put This in Your LOI\nHi Sara,\nLet\u2019s play a game. What\u2019s one thing you can put in your Letter of Intent that instantly makes a seller question your ability to run anything, much less their business?\nAnswer: A 0% interest seller note.\nYikes.\nI see this all the time. Some eager buyer (probably fresh off a YouTube binge) sends in an LOI offering seller financing at 0% interest\u2014as if that\u2019s a totally normal, savvy move.\u00a0\nSpoiler: it\u2019s not usually.\nHere\u2019s why that \u201cinterest-free\u201d offer makes sellers cringe (and quietly blacklist you):\nIt\u2019s a tax trap.\n\nEven if the seller agrees to 0%, the IRS doesn\u2019t. Imputed interest means the seller still pays taxes as if they earned interest. So you're not just offering a bad deal\u2014you're offering one that costs them.\n\nIt signals you don\u2019t understand deals.\n\nOr at least, you haven't Googled \u201capplicable federal rate.\u201d Offering a loan below that rate without understanding the tax consequences doesn\u2019t scream \"trustworthy operator of a tax firm.\"\n\nIt kills motivation to repay.\n\n Would you rush to pay off an interest-free loan? Neither would your seller. That\u2019s why they\u2019re unlikely to love the idea of giving you one.\n\nIt\u2019s not 2010.\n\nInflation is real. Cost of capital is real. And unless your seller is feeling wildly philanthropic, they need a very good reason why they should finance your dream at 0%.\n\nThe fix?\u00a0\nAt a minimum, offer AFR (Applicable Federal Rate) on seller notes. Show the seller that you understand basic finance, tax implications, and how not to look like a rookie.\nNot sure what AFR is or how to structure a seller note that doesn't make you look like a walking red flag? You can watch one of my recent videos right here.\nI\u2019ll walk you through it, no fluff.\nTo smarter offers and fewer declined LOIs,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2026\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
